tration. A node every line passes through is a bottleneck.\"},\"lineage\":{\"question\":\"What led to this outcome, and who was involved at each step?\",\"decision\":\"Read left to right. Every point is an envelope on the chain; a human lane with no point on it is a step nobody signed off.\"}},\"briefs\":[{\"name\":\"overrides\",\"title\":\"How often the agent's work is changed\",\"headline\":\"Reviewers changed 32% of 414 decided tasks: 32% corrected (28% to 37%) and 0% sent back.\",\"text\":\"68% of the agent's work went out as drafted. Of the corrections that said which, 57% refined the agent's decision and 43% reversed it (77 against 57, 0 unstated).\",\"decision\":\"Corrections split between wording and substance: look at the tags and paths to separate them.\",\"sufficient\":true,\"numbers\":{\"n\":414,\"override_rate\":0.32367149758454106,\"reject_rate\":0.0}},{\"name\":\"paths\",\"title\":\"Where the corrections land\",\"headline\":\"The most corrected part of the artefact is reply in classification tasks: 21 of 52 corrections of that kind (40%).\",\"text\":\"Across 3 task kinds, corrections touch 4 distinct parts of the artefact. The heatmap ranks them per kind, and the rationales behind any cell are one call away.\",\"decision\":\"Start with the prompt section that produces reply for classification.\",\"sufficient\":true,\"numbers\":{\"top_path\":\"reply\",\"task_kind\":\"classification\",\"share\":0.40384615384615385}},{\"name\":\"calibration\",\"title\":\"Whether confidence can be trusted\",\"headline\":\"Expected calibration error 0.09 over 414 tasks; Brier score 0.21.\",\"text\":\"The agent is overconfident: at a reported 86% reviewers accepted 75% (83 tasks). Its stated confidence runs ahead of its record.\",\"decision\":\"Set routing thresholds from the observed acceptance at each confidence level rather than the reported number.\",\"sufficient\":true,\"numbers\":{\"n\":414,\"ece\":0.08811594202898551,\"brier\":0.20692173913043477}},{\"name\":\"promotion\",\"title\":\"Whether an agent is ready to promote\",\"headline\":\"agent:drafter: 57 substantive corrections in 414 decided tasks, true rate 11% to 17% (90% credible), 1% chance it is under 10%.\",\"text\":\"The bar is a substantive correction rate under 10%: overrides that reversed the agent's decision plus rejections, out of decided tasks. With 414 decided tasks the posterior is well pinned down.\",\"decision\":\"Hold. Either the rate is above the bar or too few tasks have been decided to say.\",\"sufficient\":true,\"numbers\":{\"threshold\":0.1}},{\"name\":\"latency\",\"title\":\"How long decisions take\",\"headline\":\"Half of the reviews were decided within 1.0 hours, nine in ten within 3.9 hours; 6 still waiting.\",\"text\":\"414 review passes reached a decision. The oldest open review has waited 1.9 hours. human:ana takes longest at a median of 1.2 hours; human:ben is quickest at 57 minutes.\",\"decision\":\"Decisions are keeping up with the work.\",\"sufficient\":true,\"numbers\":{\"median_s\":3614.0,\"p90_s\":13936.8,\"open\":6}},{\"name\":\"agreement\",\"title\":\"Whether reviewers agree\",\"headline\":\"On 77 passes two reviewers decided, kappa is -0.07 (observed agreement 87%).\",\"text\":\"These are passes a first reviewer accepted, since a correction settles a pass; kappa here says how often the next reviewer agreed with an acceptance. The pair that agrees least is human:ben and human:cal (kappa -0.07 over 26 passes).\",\"decision\":\"Reviewers agree on nearly every shared pass. Kappa is low only because almost all of those passes are acceptances, which leaves little disagreement to measure.\",\"sufficient\":true,\"numbers\":{}},{\"name\":\"whispers\",\"title\":\"Whether agents get answers\",\"headline\":\"71 questions asked, 19 lapsed (27%, 18% to 38%); answers took a median of 8 minutes.\",\"text\":\"That is one question per 6 tasks.\",\"decision\":\"More than a quarter lapse: the default answer is deciding those questions. Put the answer in the